cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, data, or methodology in academic research or mission planning, please cite it as below."
title: "LightPath: Lunar South-Pole Solar Illumination, Direct-to-Earth Line of Sight, and Space-Time Route Solver"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/[team-to-fill]/lightpath"
url: "https://[team-to-fill].github.io/lightpath/"
abstract: >-
  LightPath computes topocentric solar disc illumination, lunar terrain horizon occultation,
  and Direct-to-Earth (DTE) communication line of sight for lunar south-pole exploration sites.
  It includes a spatio-temporal route solver navigating moving polar shadows and provides
  deterministic, reproducible open datasets in CSV and Apache Parquet formats.
keywords:
  - "lunar south pole"
  - "solar illumination"
  - "direct-to-earth line of sight"
  - "CLPS lunar mission browser"
  - "spatio-temporal route planning"
  - "astrodynamics"
